IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P4-gate`

-- P4-art-31-32: Article 31 (Requirements relating to notified bodies) and Article 32 (Presumption of conformity).
-- Neither article was changed by the Omnibus (marker `▼B`): one text, both versions. Every function takes `the date asked` first
-- and answers NOTHING before Chapter III Section 4 applies (2 August 2025).
-- Article 31 states what a notified body must be: most paragraphs are standing requirements (a state, not an act), so they are decision
-- functions over the facts the body can state. The three paragraphs that name an act (31(6) document and implement; 31(9) take out
-- insurance; 31(12) participate) are also regulative rules, with no time limit and no consequence stated.

§ `Article 31: the party and acts of the regulative rules`

DECLARE `Art 31 party` IS ONE OF
    `Art 31 notified body`

DECLARE `Art 31 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 31(6) document and implement a structure and procedures to safeguard impartiality`
    `Art 31(9) take out appropriate liability insurance for the conformity assessment activities`
    `Art 31(12) participate in coordination activities as referred to in Article 38`

§ `Article 31(1): established under national law, with legal personality`

-- src:569 | 1. A notified body shall be established under the national law of a Member State and shall have legal personality.
@ref Art 31(1) (src:569)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the notified body is established under the national law of a Member State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notified body has legal personality` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 31(1) the notified body is established as required` MEANS
    `Art 28 to 39 the answer when the group applies` `the date asked`
        (`the notified body is established under the national law of a Member State` AND `the notified body has legal personality`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A notified body shall be established under the national law of a Member State and shall have legal personality" (a bare "shall" not done)

§ `Article 31(2): organisational, quality management, resources, process and cybersecurity requirements`

-- src:570 | 2. Notified bodies shall satisfy the organisational, quality management, resources and process requirements that are necessary to fulfil their tasks, as well as suitable cybersecurity requirements.
@ref Art 31(2) (src:570)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the notified body satisfies the organisational, quality management, resources and process requirements that are necessary to fulfil its tasks` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notified body satisfies suitable cybersecurity requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 31(2) the notified body satisfies the requirements as required` MEANS
    `Art 28 to 39 the answer when the group applies` `the date asked`
        (   `the notified body satisfies the organisational, quality management, resources and process requirements that are necessary to fulfil its tasks`
        AND `the notified body satisfies suitable cybersecurity requirements`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Notified bodies shall satisfy the organisational, quality management, resources and process requirements that are necessary to fulfil their tasks, as well as suitable cybersecurity requirements" (a bare "shall" not done)

§ `Article 31(3): confidence in performance and results`

-- src:571 | 3. The organisational structure, allocation of responsibilities, reporting lines and operation of notified bodies shall ensure confidence in their performance, and in the results of the conformity assessment activities that the notified bodies conduct.
@ref Art 31(3) (src:571)
-- Gloss: the way the body is organised and works must give confidence in how it performs and in the results of its conformity assessment. Whether it does is a judgment the text leaves open: taken as an input.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the organisational structure, allocation of responsibilities, reporting lines and operation of the notified body ensure confidence in its performance and in the results of the conformity assessment activities it conducts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 31(3) the organisational structure ensures confidence` MEANS
    `Art 28 to 39 the answer when the group applies` `the date asked`
        (`the organisational structure, allocation of responsibilities, reporting lines and operation of the notified body ensure confidence in its performance and in the results of the conformity assessment activities it conducts`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The organisational structure, allocation of responsibilities, reporting lines and operation of notified bodies shall ensure confidence in their performance" (a bare "shall" not done)

§ `Article 31(4): independence`

-- src:572 | 4. Notified bodies shall be independent of the provider of a high-risk AI system in relation to which they perform conformity assessment activities. Notified bodies shall also be independent of any other operator having an economic interest in high-risk AI systems assessed, as well as of any competitors of the provider. This shall not preclude the use of assessed high-risk AI systems that are necessary for the operations of the conformity assessment body, or the use of such high-risk AI systems for personal purposes.
@ref Art 31(4) (src:572)
-- Gloss: independent of the provider whose high-risk AI system it assesses, of any other operator with an economic interest in the systems assessed, and of the provider's competitors.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the notified body is independent of the provider of the high-risk AI system in relation to which it performs conformity assessment activities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notified body is independent of any other operator having an economic interest in the high-risk AI systems assessed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notified body is independent of any competitors of the provider` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 31(4) first and second sentences the notified body is independent` MEANS
    `Art 28 to 39 the answer when the group applies` `the date asked`
        (   `the notified body is independent of the provider of the high-risk AI system in relation to which it performs conformity assessment activities`
        AND `the notified body is independent of any other operator having an economic interest in the high-risk AI systems assessed`
        AND `the notified body is independent of any competitors of the provider`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Notified bodies shall be independent of the provider ... shall also be independent of any other operator having an economic interest ..., as well as of any competitors of the provider" (a bare "shall" not done)

-- src:572 | 4. Notified bodies shall be independent of the provider of a high-risk AI system in relation to which they perform conformity assessment activities. Notified bodies shall also be independent of any other operator having an economic interest in high-risk AI systems assessed, as well as of any competitors of the provider. This shall not preclude the use of assessed high-risk AI systems that are necessary for the operations of the conformity assessment body, or the use of such high-risk AI systems for personal purposes.
@ref Art 31(4) (src:572)
-- Gloss: using the assessed high-risk AI systems because the body needs them for its operations, or for personal purposes, is not ruled out by the independence requirement.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the use is of assessed high-risk AI systems that are necessary for the operations of the conformity assessment body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is of such high-risk AI systems for personal purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 31(4) third sentence the independence requirement precludes the use of the assessed high-risk AI system` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 4 applies from 2 August 2025
    ELSE IF `the use is of assessed high-risk AI systems that are necessary for the operations of the conformity assessment body` OR `the use is of such high-risk AI systems for personal purposes`
         THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This shall not preclude the use of assessed high-risk AI systems that are necessary for the operations of the conformity assessment body, or the use of such high-risk AI systems for personal purposes" (a flat negative)
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): any other use of an assessed system is not addressed by this sentence; the first two sentences govern it

§ `Article 31(5): no involvement in design, development, marketing or use; no conflicting activity`

-- src:573 | 5. Neither a conformity assessment body, its top-level management nor the personnel responsible for carrying out its conformity assessment tasks shall be directly involved in the design, development, marketing or use of high-risk AI systems, nor shall they represent the parties engaged in those activities. They shall not engage in any activity that might conflict with their independence of judgement or integrity in relation to conformity assessment activities for which they are notified. This shall, in particular, apply to consultancy services.
@ref Art 31(5) (src:573)
-- Gloss: neither the body, its top management nor the staff who do the assessments may be directly involved in designing, developing, marketing or using high-risk AI systems or represent those who are, nor engage in anything that might conflict with their independence of judgement or integrity, consultancy services above all.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the conformity assessment body, its top-level management or the personnel responsible for carrying out its conformity assessment tasks are directly involved in the design, development, marketing or use of high-risk AI systems` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they represent the parties engaged in those activities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they engage in an activity that might conflict with their independence of judgement or integrity in relation to the conformity assessment activities for which they are notified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they provide consultancy services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 31(5) the conformity assessment body, its management and its personnel have kept to the bar on involvement and conflicting activity` MEANS
    `Art 28 to 39 the answer when the group applies` `the date asked`
        (   (NOT `the conformity assessment body, its top-level management or the personnel responsible for carrying out its conformity assessment tasks are directly involved in the design, development, marketing or use of high-risk AI systems`)
        AND (NOT `they represent the parties engaged in those activities`)
        AND (NOT `they engage in an activity that might conflict with their independence of judgement or integrity in relation to the conformity assessment activities for which they are notified`)
        AND (NOT `they provide consultancy services`))
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Neither a conformity assessment body, its top-level management nor the personnel ... shall be directly involved in the design, development, marketing or use of high-risk AI systems, nor shall they represent the parties engaged in those activities. They shall not engage in any activity that might conflict with their independence of judgement or integrity ... This shall, in particular, apply to consultancy services" (a flat negative)

§ `Article 31(6): organised and operated to safeguard independence and impartiality`

-- src:574 | 6. Notified bodies shall be organised and operated so as to safeguard the independence, objectivity and impartiality of their activities. Notified bodies shall document and implement a structure and procedures to safeguard impartiality and to promote and apply the principles of impartiality throughout their organisation, personnel and assessment activities.
@ref Art 31(6) (src:574)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the notified body is organised and operated so as to safeguard the independence, objectivity and impartiality of its activities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notified body has documented a structure and procedures to safeguard impartiality and to promote and apply the principles of impartiality throughout its organisation, personnel and assessment activities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notified body has implemented that structure and those procedures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 31(6) the notified body is organised and operated as required` MEANS
    `Art 28 to 39 the answer when the group applies` `the date asked`
        (   `the notified body is organised and operated so as to safeguard the independence, objectivity and impartiality of its activities`
        AND `the notified body has documented a structure and procedures to safeguard impartiality and to promote and apply the principles of impartiality throughout its organisation, personnel and assessment activities`
        AND `the notified body has implemented that structure and those procedures`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Notified bodies shall be organised and operated so as to safeguard the independence, objectivity and impartiality of their activities. Notified bodies shall document and implement a structure and procedures" (a bare "shall" not done)

-- No time limit and no consequence is stated, so no trace can show this rule breached.
-- src:574 | 6. Notified bodies shall be organised and operated so as to safeguard the independence, objectivity and impartiality of their activities. Notified bodies shall document and implement a structure and procedures to safeguard impartiality and to promote and apply the principles of impartiality throughout their organisation, personnel and assessment activities.
@ref Art 31(6) (src:574)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 31 party` `Art 31 act`
`Art 31(6) the duty of the notified body to document and implement a structure and procedures` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed before Chapter III Section 4 applies
    ELSE PARTY `Art 31 notified body`
         MUST `Art 31(6) document and implement a structure and procedures to safeguard impartiality`
         HENCE FULFILLED

§ `Article 31(7): confidentiality and professional secrecy`

-- src:575 | 7. Notified bodies shall have documented procedures in place ensuring that their personnel, committees, subsidiaries, subcontractors and any associated body or personnel of external bodies maintain, in accordance with Article 78, the confidentiality of the information which comes into their possession during the performance of conformity assessment activities, except when its disclosure is required by law. The staff of notified bodies shall be bound to observe professional secrecy with regard to all information obtained in carrying out their tasks under this Regulation, except in relation to the notifying authorities of the Member State in which their activities are carried out.
@ref Art 31(7) (src:575)
-- Gloss: written procedures so that the body's staff, committees, subsidiaries, subcontractors and associated bodies keep the information confidential as Article 78 requires, unless the law requires disclosure; and the staff are bound by professional secrecy, except towards the notifying authority of the Member State where they work. Article 78 is another part's: taken as an input (seam S-78). Each "except" clause is asked inside the fact it qualifies, not as a separate limb (fork F-31-7).
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the notified body has documented procedures in place ensuring that its personnel, committees, subsidiaries, subcontractors and any associated body or personnel of external bodies maintain, in accordance with Article 78, the confidentiality of the information which comes into their possession, except when its disclosure is required by law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the staff of the notified body are bound to observe professional secrecy with regard to all information obtained in carrying out their tasks under this Regulation, except in relation to the notifying authorities of the Member State in which their activities are carried out` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 31(7) the notified body has the procedures and the professional secrecy required` MEANS
    `Art 28 to 39 the answer when the group applies` `the date asked`
        (   `the notified body has documented procedures in place ensuring that its personnel, committees, subsidiaries, subcontractors and any associated body or personnel of external bodies maintain, in accordance with Article 78, the confidentiality of the information which comes into their possession, except when its disclosure is required by law`
        AND `the staff of the notified body are bound to observe professional secrecy with regard to all information obtained in carrying out their tasks under this Regulation, except in relation to the notifying authorities of the Member State in which their activities are carried out`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Notified bodies shall have documented procedures in place ensuring that their personnel ... maintain, in accordance with Article 78, the confidentiality ... The staff of notified bodies shall be bound to observe professional secrecy" (a bare "shall" not done)

