@ref Art 31(8) (src:576)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the notified body has procedures for the performance of activities which take due account of the size of a provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they take due account of the sector in which the provider operates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they take due account of the provider's structure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they take due account of the degree of complexity of the AI system concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 31(8) the notified body has procedures that take due account of the provider and the AI system` MEANS
    `Art 28 to 39 the answer when the group applies` `the date asked`
        (   `the notified body has procedures for the performance of activities which take due account of the size of a provider`
        AND `they take due account of the sector in which the provider operates`
        AND `they take due account of the provider's structure`
        AND `they take due account of the degree of complexity of the AI system concerned`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Notified bodies shall have procedures for the performance of activities which take due account of the size of a provider, the sector in which it operates, its structure, and the degree of complexity of the AI system concerned" (a bare "shall" not done)

§ `Article 31(9): liability insurance`

-- src:577 | 9. Notified bodies shall take out appropriate liability insurance for their conformity assessment activities, unless liability is assumed by the Member State in which they are established in accordance with national law or that Member State is itself directly responsible for the conformity assessment.
@ref Art 31(9) (src:577)
-- Gloss: the body takes out suitable liability insurance, unless the Member State where it is established takes on the liability under national law or is itself directly responsible for the conformity assessment. An "unless" that is met counts as the duty met: JUST TRUE (fork F-31-9).
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the notified body has taken out appropriate liability insurance for its conformity assessment activities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `liability is assumed by the Member State in which the notified body is established in accordance with national law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that Member State is itself directly responsible for the conformity assessment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 31(9) the notified body has the liability insurance required` MEANS
    `Art 28 to 39 the answer when the group applies` `the date asked`
        (   `the notified body has taken out appropriate liability insurance for its conformity assessment activities`
         OR `liability is assumed by the Member State in which the notified body is established in accordance with national law`
         OR `that Member State is itself directly responsible for the conformity assessment`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall take out appropriate liability insurance for their conformity assessment activities, unless liability is assumed by the Member State ... or that Member State is itself directly responsible for the conformity assessment" (an "unless" not met)

-- No time limit and no consequence is stated, so no trace can show this rule breached.
-- src:577 | 9. Notified bodies shall take out appropriate liability insurance for their conformity assessment activities, unless liability is assumed by the Member State in which they are established in accordance with national law or that Member State is itself directly responsible for the conformity assessment.
@ref Art 31(9) (src:577)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 31 party` `Art 31 act`
`Art 31(9) the duty of the notified body to take out liability insurance` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed before Chapter III Section 4 applies
    ELSE PARTY `Art 31 notified body`
         MUST `Art 31(9) take out appropriate liability insurance for the conformity assessment activities`
         HENCE FULFILLED

§ `Article 31(10): integrity and competence`

-- src:578 | 10. Notified bodies shall be capable of carrying out all their tasks under this Regulation with the highest degree of professional integrity and the requisite competence in the specific field, whether those tasks are carried out by notified bodies themselves or on their behalf and under their responsibility.
@ref Art 31(10) (src:578)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the notified body is capable of carrying out all its tasks under this Regulation with the highest degree of professional integrity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notified body is capable of carrying out all its tasks under this Regulation with the requisite competence in the specific field` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 31(10) the notified body is capable of carrying out all its tasks as required` MEANS
    `Art 28 to 39 the answer when the group applies` `the date asked`
        (   `the notified body is capable of carrying out all its tasks under this Regulation with the highest degree of professional integrity`
        AND `the notified body is capable of carrying out all its tasks under this Regulation with the requisite competence in the specific field`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Notified bodies shall be capable of carrying out all their tasks under this Regulation with the highest degree of professional integrity and the requisite competence in the specific field, whether those tasks are carried out by notified bodies themselves or on their behalf and under their responsibility" (a bare "shall" not done)

§ `Article 31(11): internal competences and permanent personnel`

-- src:579 | 11. Notified bodies shall have sufficient internal competences to be able effectively to evaluate the tasks conducted by external parties on their behalf. The notified body shall have permanent availability of sufficient administrative, technical, legal and scientific personnel who possess experience and knowledge relating to the relevant types of AI systems, data and data computing, and relating to the requirements set out in Section 2.
@ref Art 31(11) (src:579)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the notified body has sufficient internal competences to be able effectively to evaluate the tasks conducted by external parties on its behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notified body has permanent availability of sufficient administrative, technical, legal and scientific personnel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that personnel possess experience and knowledge relating to the relevant types of AI systems, data and data computing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that personnel possess experience and knowledge relating to the requirements set out in Section 2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 31(11) the notified body has the internal competences and the permanent personnel required` MEANS
    `Art 28 to 39 the answer when the group applies` `the date asked`
        (   `the notified body has sufficient internal competences to be able effectively to evaluate the tasks conducted by external parties on its behalf`
        AND `the notified body has permanent availability of sufficient administrative, technical, legal and scientific personnel`
        AND `that personnel possess experience and knowledge relating to the relevant types of AI systems, data and data computing`
        AND `that personnel possess experience and knowledge relating to the requirements set out in Section 2`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Notified bodies shall have sufficient internal competences ... The notified body shall have permanent availability of sufficient administrative, technical, legal and scientific personnel" (a bare "shall" not done)

§ `Article 31(12): coordination and standards`

-- src:580 | 12. Notified bodies shall participate in coordination activities as referred to in Article 38. They shall also take part directly, or be represented in, European standardisation organisations, or ensure that they are aware and up to date in respect of relevant standards.
@ref Art 31(12) (src:580)
-- Gloss: the body takes part in the coordination activities of Article 38, and either takes part in (or is represented in) the European standardisation organisations or makes sure it is aware of and up to date with the relevant standards.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the notified body participates in coordination activities as referred to in Article 38` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notified body takes part directly in European standardisation organisations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notified body is represented in European standardisation organisations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notified body ensures that it is aware and up to date in respect of relevant standards` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 31(12) the notified body participates in coordination and keeps up with standards as required` MEANS
    `Art 28 to 39 the answer when the group applies` `the date asked`
        (   `the notified body participates in coordination activities as referred to in Article 38`
        AND (   `the notified body takes part directly in European standardisation organisations`
             OR `the notified body is represented in European standardisation organisations`
             OR `the notified body ensures that it is aware and up to date in respect of relevant standards`))
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Notified bodies shall participate in coordination activities as referred to in Article 38. They shall also take part directly, or be represented in, European standardisation organisations, or ensure that they are aware and up to date in respect of relevant standards" (a bare "shall" not done)

-- No time limit and no consequence is stated, so no trace can show this rule breached.
