§ `Article 31: the requirements as a whole, from the answers of the paragraphs`

-- Article 30(1) turns on whether the body "has satisfied the requirements laid down in Article 31". This takes the answers of the twelve
-- paragraphs (the sentences of 31(4) and (5) are within their paragraphs) and says: all satisfied, none unmet, or not covered. A caller must never
-- turn a NOTHING into a FALSE. An empty list is not an answer: NOTHING.
GIVEN `the answers of the paragraphs` IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 31 the notified body has satisfied the requirements given the answers of the paragraphs` MEANS
    IF `the answers of the paragraphs` EQUALS EMPTY
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no paragraph was answered
    ELSE IF any (GIVEN `an answer` YIELD `an answer` EQUALS JUST FALSE) `the answers of the paragraphs`
         THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): a paragraph of Article 31 that the body does not meet is a requirement of Article 31 not satisfied
         ELSE IF all (GIVEN `an answer` YIELD `an answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE) `the answers of the paragraphs`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): at least one paragraph is not answered on the facts given, and none is unmet

§ `Article 32: presumption of conformity with the requirements relating to notified bodies`

-- src:583 | Where a conformity assessment body demonstrates its conformity with the criteria laid down in the relevant harmonised standards or parts thereof, the references of which have been published in the Official Journal of the European Union, it shall be presumed to comply with the requirements set out in Article 31 in so far as the applicable harmonised standards cover those requirements.
@ref Art 32 (src:583)
-- Gloss: a body that meets the criteria of the relevant harmonised standards, whose references are published in the Official Journal, is presumed to meet the Article 31 requirements those standards cover.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the conformity assessment body demonstrates its conformity with the criteria laid down in the relevant harmonised standards or parts thereof` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the references of those harmonised standards have been published in the Official Journal of the European Union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicable harmonised standards cover the requirement set out in Article 31` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 32 the conformity assessment body is presumed to comply with the requirement set out in Article 31` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 4 applies from 2 August 2025
    ELSE IF (NOT `the conformity assessment body demonstrates its conformity with the criteria laid down in the relevant harmonised standards or parts thereof`) OR (NOT `the references of those harmonised standards have been published in the Official Journal of the European Union`)
         THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a conformity assessment body demonstrates its conformity with the criteria laid down in the relevant harmonised standards or parts thereof, the references of which have been published in the Official Journal of the European Union" (a "where" condition that fails: the periods ruling's rule (b); not a duty and not a "may"; fork F-32-where)
         ELSE IF `the applicable harmonised standards cover the requirement set out in Article 31`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in so far as the applicable harmonised standards cover those requirements" (a scope limit with no "only": the periods ruling's rule (c); fork F-32-where)
